++### How to set the `fields` parameter
++
++Look at the user's question and match it to the patterns below to pick the right `fields` value.
++
++---
++
++#### Smart defaults (apply these BEFORE selecting fields — never ask the user)
++
++| Ambiguity | Default assumption |
++|---|---|
++| No year specified | `assessment_year="2026"` (fall back to `"2025"` if all N/A) |
++| "ratings" without specifying whose | Include BOTH `self_rating` AND `direct_manager_rating` |
++| "comments" without specifying whose | Include BOTH `self_comments` AND `manager_comments` |
++| "top performers" without a count | Return top **5** sorted by `band_numeric` desc / `manager_validated_final_kra_score` desc |
++| "bottom performers" without a count | Return bottom **5** sorted by `band_numeric` asc |
++| "reportees" without direct/practice qualifier | Use `search_by_manager` (direct reports) |
++| "performance" / "review" / "appraisal" (vague) | Use fields: `emp_name,category_band,band_numeric,manager_validated_final_kra_score,separation_status` |
++| "summary" / "overview" for an individual | Use `search_by_employee` with `fields="all"` — **Exception: if the query also mentions "goals", "objectives", or "weightage", use the Goals routing row instead of this default.** |
++| Employee name is ambiguous (partial match) | Return data for ALL matching employees; let the user pick from results rather than asking "which one?" |
++
++---
++
++#### Reportee listing & identity
++
++| Question pattern | `fields` to use |
++|---|---|
++| "list reportees" / "who reports to me" (no specific field) | `emp_name` |
++| "reportees with their competency / grade" | `emp_name,competency` |
++| "reportees with their BU / business unit" | `emp_name,BU` |
++| "reportees with competency and BU" | `emp_name,competency,BU` |
++| "who joined in [month/quarter/year]" | `emp_name,joined_date,category_band` |
++| "members promoted last year / recently promoted" | `emp_name,promotion_date,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score` |
++| "resigned / separated employees" | `emp_name,separation_status,category_band` |
++
++---
++
++#### Performance bands & ranking
++
++| Question pattern | `fields` to use |
++|---|---|
++| "top and bottom performers" / "rank by band" / "who is EC/SC/CC/IC/NC" / "band distribution" / "predict band distribution" | `emp_name,category_band,band_numeric,manager_validated_final_kra_score,separation_status` |
++| "list all members rated EC or SC" / "high performers" | `emp_name,category_band,band_numeric,separation_status` |
++| "list all members rated IC or NC" / "bottom performers" / "at-risk members" | `emp_name,category_band,band_numeric,separation_status` |
++| "highest KRA score" / "who has the highest score" | `emp_name,category_band,band_numeric,manager_validated_final_kra_score` |
++| "band distribution for members who joined in Q[N] FY[YY]" | `emp_name,joined_date,category_band,band_numeric,separation_status` |
++
++---
++
++#### Rating comparisons
++
++> ℹ️ `self_rating_avg`, `manager_rating_avg`, `practice_manager_rating_avg`, and `rating_self_mgr_gap` are pre-computed employee-level averages stored in the index (average across all objectives). A positive `rating_self_mgr_gap` means the employee rated themselves higher than the manager. For 2026, `manager_rating_avg` and `rating_self_mgr_gap` will be `\N` if the manager has not yet finalized ratings.
++
++| Question pattern | `fields` to use |
++|---|---|
++| "self-rating vs manager rating" / "comparison of ratings" / "self vs mgr" / "highlight self-assessment outliers" | `emp_name,self_rating_avg,manager_rating_avg,rating_self_mgr_gap,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score` |
++| "practice manager rating comparison" | `emp_name,self_rating_avg,manager_rating_avg,practice_manager_rating_avg,rating_self_mgr_gap,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score` |
++| "performance summary of all reportees" / "overall ratings for team" | `emp_name,category_band,manager_validated_final_kra_score,self_rating_avg,manager_rating_avg,rating_self_mgr_gap,separation_status` |
++
++---
++
++#### Goals, objectives & achievement
++
