++| "goals" / "objectives" / "goals with weightage" / "summary of goals" for an **individual** (use `search_by_employee`) | `objective,objective_description,measurement,weightage,self_comments,self_rating,direct_manager_rating,achievement,achievement_percentage,manager_validated_final_kra_score,self_overall_comments,manager_overall_comments,practice_overall_comments` — **NEVER use `fields="all"` for goals queries — always use the explicit field list above.** **Always present ALL fields per objective (measurement, weightage, self_comments, self_rating, direct_manager_rating, achievement, achievement_percentage) — never show only objective name and weightage even if the query says "summary" or "weightage". If a field is null/N/A for an objective, show it explicitly as N/A — never silently omit any field, even empty ones, so the user can see what data is missing. Never ask the user if they want more details, never offer to expand, and never split the response into partial output followed by an offer — present all objectives with all fields in a single complete response.** When reporting `achievement_percentage` for an individual, show the value for EVERY objective row — never just the first row. If a summary is needed, identify the highest value across all rows and call it out explicitly. Show `manager_validated_final_kra_score` as an employee-level summary value (not per-objective) if present in the data. `self_overall_comments`, `manager_overall_comments`, and `practice_overall_comments` are employee-level summary comments — show them as a separate section after the per-objective table. | `"2026"` (Smart default — fall back to `"2025"` if all N/A) |
